# Decode loop semantics — PML5-U1 (production inference computation layer).
#
# Public import: importa ex "gradus:decode" privata decode
# Depends on: gradus:dtype (finita), gradus:tensor (value carrier),
# gradus:nn (linear — the output projection), gradus:transformer
# (transformer_block — the SHARED forward row).
#
# Architectural rule: gradus owns computation and logical state — NOT
# scheduling, batching, HTTP, or device handles (the product repo / NGAB
# own those). This module holds no backend or device handle and makes no
# performance claims (NGAB owns executable evidence).
#
# =========================================================================
# The decode contract (pml5-delivery.md PML5-U1)
# =========================================================================
#
# --- One-token decode over the forward row -------------------------------
# decodere_datum(token_id, positio, decodere) is the explicit public
# one-token decode op: token id + position in → full-vocabulary logits
# out. The forward row is the PML3 shared transformer block
# (transformer.transformer_block, attention mode 2 — causal + RoPE, the
# selected inference row) over the F32 staged carrier; the decode composes
# embedding gather → block → output projection.
#
# --- Prefill and decode share the same forward functions -----------------
# praefundere(tokens, decodere) runs the multi-token (teacher-forced)
# path over the SAME forward functions: the same embedding gather, the
# same transformer_block, the same output projection. The single-token
# prefill IS the decode at position 0 (probed); the first prefill
# position equals the single-token decode at position 0 (probed). The
# decode's single-token causal self-score is position-invariant under RoPE
# (the rotation of q and k by the same angles cancels in the dot product)
# — the position enters through the multi-token causal path (and the
# KV-cache of U2).
#
# --- Reset / context-limit behavior (explicit) ---------------------------
# The Decodere declares its context length (contextus); the decode op and
# the prefill op fail closed on positions at or beyond it (reject policy —
# no silent truncation; U5 owns the full session policy). The session
# (Sessio) is an explicit position counter with advance (progredere —
# rejects at the limit) and reset (redintegra — back to position 0);
# no hidden position state.
#
# --- Oracle-matching logits (GI2 contract, read-only inputs) -------------
# The logits are pinned per the GI2 numeric-contract discipline (read
# only: gi0-numeric-contract.md — full-vocab raw logits, finite gate,
# top-1 exactness on each pin row, first-divergence rule) applied to
# the gradus forward row: the decode.proba pins f64 evaluations of the
# documented forward arithmetic (the same arithmetic the transformer/
# attention/nn probas pin) with the documented 5e-4 tolerance. The GI2
# oracle itself (dequant + the 32-layer decoder in faber-runtime) is a
# read-only input to this phase, never reimplemented here.
#
# --- Evidence honesty (CTO Q2, hard) -------------------------------------
# This surface is the STRUCTURAL proof: the decode op, the prefill/decode
# sharing, and the reset/limit behavior are compile-validated and proven
# by the co-located proba (f64 oracle pins). Executed VALUE identity
# (the logits computed at runtime) is env-blocked tree-wide today (FMIR
# stepper / library-import gap — the PML4 closeout recorded both blockers;
# neither is fixed here). PML5-U1 is PARTIAL: logit-value identity is
# deferred to the auditor-owned runtime-evidence gate.
#
# =========================================================================
# PML5-U5 additions — reset, cancellation observation, deterministic replay
# =========================================================================
#
# --- Session reset (fresh state) -----------------------------------------
# redintegra(Sessio) resets an advanced session to position 0, preserving
# the context limit — the public reset. The generation cursor
# (generation.fab) wires it as the cursor reset.
#
# --- Cancellation observation points (cooperative, fail closed) ----------
# Cancelatum is an explicit pure value; observa_cancellationem is the
# cooperative checkpoint the generation loop calls at step boundaries. A
# set flag REJECTS with Cancelata (typed) — cancellation is observed, never
# assumed, never silently skipped. The decode/replay compositions observe
# the flag at entry and before every step.
#
# --- Deterministic replay (same seed + input -> same tokens) -------------
# replica(logits-stream, sampling Configura, history, Semen, Cancelatum)
# is the bounded deterministic sampling composition: per-step
# sampling.sors over the running history with the explicit advancing RNG
# state. Pure — equal inputs produce equal token sequences (probed). The
# model decode (logits production) is NOT here — U6 wires decodere_datum
# into the aggregate.
#
# --- No server / device handle --------------------------------------------
# This module holds no device handle, no server, no HTTP/batching
# surface — only logical state (sessions, cancellation tokens, the replay
# composition). No performance claims.
importa ex "gradus:dtype" dtype
importa ex "gradus:tensor" tensor
importa ex "gradus:nn" nn
importa ex "gradus:transformer" transformer
importa ex "gradus:sampling" sampling
importa ex "gradus:train" train

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DecodeError — typed error vocabulary of the decode surface.
# Every variant carries a textus causa (render via causa).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

discretio DecodeError {
    IdExtra { textus causa },
    PositioInvalida { textus causa },
    Terminus { textus causa },
    DecodereInvalida { textus causa },
    FormaMismatch { textus causa },
    TypoMismatch { textus causa },
    ElementaMismatch { textus causa },
    Incompatibilis { textus causa },
    DimensioInvalida { textus causa },
    Cancelata { textus causa },
    SamplingDefecta { textus causa }
}

@ publica
functio causa(DecodeError e) → textus {
    discerne e {
        casu IdExtra fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu PositioInvalida fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu Terminus fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu DecodereInvalida fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu FormaMismatch fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu TypoMismatch fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu ElementaMismatch fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu Incompatibilis fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu DimensioInvalida fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu Cancelata fixum causa { redde causa }
        casu SamplingDefecta fixum causa { redde causa }
    }
}

# The attention mode of the shared forward row: 2 = causal + RoPE (the
# selected inference row, transformer.fab mode contract).
fixum numerus MODUS_INFERENTIA ← 2

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pondera — the transformer block's weights (the shared forward row's
# parameters). Mirrors the transformer_block argument order.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
genus Pondera {
    tensor.Tensor ln1_s
    tensor.Tensor ln1_o
    tensor.Tensor wq
    tensor.Tensor bq
    tensor.Tensor wk
    tensor.Tensor bk
    tensor.Tensor wv
    tensor.Tensor bv
    tensor.Tensor wo
    tensor.Tensor bo
    tensor.Tensor ln2_s
    tensor.Tensor ln2_o
    tensor.Tensor wf1
    tensor.Tensor bf1
    tensor.Tensor wf2
    tensor.Tensor bf2
    tensor.Tensor ln3_s
    tensor.Tensor ln3_o

    functio ln1_s() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.ln1_s }
    functio ln1_o() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.ln1_o }
    functio wq() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.wq }
    functio bq() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.bq }
    functio wk() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.wk }
    functio bk() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.bk }
    functio wv() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.wv }
    functio bv() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.bv }
    functio wo() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.wo }
    functio bo() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.bo }
    functio ln2_s() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.ln2_s }
    functio ln2_o() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.ln2_o }
    functio wf1() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.wf1 }
    functio bf1() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.bf1 }
    functio wf2() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.wf2 }
    functio bf2() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.bf2 }
    functio ln3_s() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.ln3_s }
    functio ln3_o() → tensor.Tensor { redde ego.ln3_o }
}

# Build the block weights (the block's own fail-closed validation runs at
# call time; the decode-level invariants are the Decodere constructor's).
@ publica
functio structa_pondera(
    tensor.Tensor ln1_s, tensor.Tensor ln1_o,
    tensor.Tensor wq, tensor.Tensor bq,
    tensor.Tensor wk, tensor.Tensor bk,
    tensor.Tensor wv, tensor.Tensor bv,
    tensor.Tensor wo, tensor.Tensor bo,
    tensor.Tensor ln2_s, tensor.Tensor ln2_o,
    tensor.Tensor wf1, tensor.Tensor bf1,
    tensor.Tensor wf2, tensor.Tensor bf2,
    tensor.Tensor ln3_s, tensor.Tensor ln3_o
) → Pondera {
    redde Pondera {
        ln1_s = ln1_s, ln1_o = ln1_o,
        wq = wq, bq = bq, wk = wk, bk = bk, wv = wv, bv = bv,
        wo = wo, bo = bo,
        ln2_s = ln2_s, ln2_o = ln2_o,
        wf1 = wf1, bf1 = bf1, wf2 = wf2, bf2 = bf2,
        ln3_s = ln3_s, ln3_o = ln3_o
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decodere — the model handle: the embedding table + the block weights +
# the output projection + the decode configuration. Gradus owns this
# logical state; no device handle. The forward row's weight-shape
# validation is the transformer_block's fail-closed contract (call time);
# this constructor validates the decode-level invariants.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
genus Decodere {
    tensor.Tensor mensa
    Pondera pondera
    tensor.Tensor projectio
    tensor.Tensor projectio_bias
    f32 scala
    numerus vocabulum
    numerus contextus
    numerus dimensio

    # The embedding table [vocabulum, dimensio].
    functio mensa() → tensor.Tensor {
        redde ego.mensa
    }

    # The shared forward row's block weights.
    functio pondera() → Pondera {
        redde ego.pondera
    }

    # The output projection [dimensio, vocabulum].
    functio projectio() → tensor.Tensor {
        redde ego.projectio
    }

    # The output projection bias [vocabulum].
    functio projectio_bias() → tensor.Tensor {
        redde ego.projectio_bias
    }

    # The attention dk scaling factor (1/sqrt(dk)).
    functio scala() → f32 {
        redde ego.scala
    }

    # Vocabulary size (token-id domain [0, vocabulum)).
    functio vocabulum() → numerus {
        redde ego.vocabulum
    }

    # Context length (the position limit; decode fails closed at it).
    functio contextus() → numerus {
        redde ego.contextus
    }

    # Embedding dimension (the forward row's feature width).
    functio dimensio() → numerus {
        redde ego.dimensio
    }
}

@ publica
functio structa_decodere(
    tensor.Tensor mensa,
    Pondera pondera,
    tensor.Tensor projectio,
    tensor.Tensor projectio_bias,
    f32 scala,
    numerus vocabulum,
    numerus contextus,
    numerus dimensio
) → Decodere ⇥ DecodeError {
    si vocabulum < 1 {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "vocabulary must be non-empty" }
    }
    si contextus < 1 {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "context length must be at least one" }
    }
    si dimensio < 1 {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "embedding dimension must be at least one" }
    }
    si non (dtype.finita(scala)) {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "invalid attention scale" }
    }
    si scala ≤ 0.0 {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "invalid attention scale" }
    }
    fixum lista<numerus> fm ← mensa.figura()
    si fm.longitudo() ≠ 2 {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "embedding must be rank-2" }
    }
    si (fm.accipe(0) vel 1) ≠ vocabulum {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "embedding rows must equal the vocabulary" }
    }
    si (fm.accipe(1) vel 1) ≠ dimensio {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "embedding columns must equal the dimension" }
    }
    fixum lista<numerus> fp ← projectio.figura()
    si fp.longitudo() ≠ 2 {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "output projection must be rank-2" }
    }
    si (fp.accipe(0) vel 1) ≠ dimensio aut (fp.accipe(1) vel 1) ≠ vocabulum {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "output projection shape must be [dim, vocab]" }
    }
    fixum lista<numerus> fpb ← projectio_bias.figura()
    si fpb.longitudo() ≠ 1 aut (fpb.accipe(0) vel 1) ≠ vocabulum {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "output projection bias must be [vocab]" }
    }
    redde Decodere {
        mensa = mensa,
        pondera = pondera,
        projectio = projectio,
        projectio_bias = projectio_bias,
        scala = scala,
        vocabulum = vocabulum,
        contextus = contextus,
        dimensio = dimensio
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private helpers.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Staged-tensor construction (the never-firing shape check, re-mapped).
@ privata
functio _tense(lista<f32> datos, lista<numerus> forma) → tensor.Tensor ⇥ DecodeError {
    fac {
        redde tensor.structa(datos, forma)
    }
    cape err {
        iace finge ElementaMismatch { causa = tensor.causa(err) }
    }
    iace finge ElementaMismatch { causa = "unreachable" }
}

# The embedding gather: the token's row of the embedding table, flat.
@ privata
functio _immersio(tensor.Tensor mensa, numerus id, numerus dim) → lista<f32> {
    varia lista<f32> row ← vacua
    varia numerus i ← 0
    dum i < dim {
        row.appende(mensa.datos.accipe(id * dim + i) vel (0.0 ∷ f32))
        i ← i + 1
    }
    redde row
}

# The shared forward row: the transformer block (mode 2 — causal + RoPE)
# over the staged carrier, positions explicit.
@ privata
functio _bloccum(Decodere m, tensor.Tensor x, lista<numerus> positions) → tensor.Tensor ⇥ DecodeError {
    fixum Pondera p ← m.pondera()
    fac {
        redde transformer.transformer_block(
            x,
            p.ln1_s(), p.ln1_o(),
            p.wq(), p.bq(),
            p.wk(), p.bk(),
            p.wv(), p.bv(),
            p.wo(), p.bo(),
            p.ln2_s(), p.ln2_o(),
            p.wf1(), p.bf1(),
            p.wf2(), p.bf2(),
            p.ln3_s(), p.ln3_o(),
            m.scala(),
            MODUS_INFERENTIA,
            positions,
            m.dimensio())
    }
    cape err {
        fixum textus c ← transformer.causa(err)
        si c ≡ "inner dimensions mismatch" {
            iace finge Incompatibilis { causa = c }
        }
        si c ≡ "dtype mismatch" {
            iace finge TypoMismatch { causa = c }
        }
        si c ≡ "bias does not match output width" {
            iace finge FormaMismatch { causa = c }
        }
        si c ≡ "unknown attention mode" {
            iace finge DimensioInvalida { causa = c }
        }
        iace finge FormaMismatch { causa = c }
    }
}

# The output projection: the block output → full-vocab logits.
@ privata
functio _projicere(Decodere m, tensor.Tensor h) → tensor.Tensor ⇥ DecodeError {
    fac {
        redde nn.linear(h, m.projectio(), m.projectio_bias())
    }
    cape err {
        fixum textus c ← nn.causa(err)
        si c ≡ "inner dimensions mismatch" {
            iace finge Incompatibilis { causa = c }
        }
        si c ≡ "dtype mismatch" {
            iace finge TypoMismatch { causa = c }
        }
        iace finge FormaMismatch { causa = c }
    }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# decodere_datum — the ONE-token decode op: token id + position in →
# full-vocab logits out, over the shared forward row. Fail closed on a
# token id outside [0, vocabulum) and a position at or beyond the context
# limit (the reject policy — no silent truncation).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
functio decodere_datum(numerus token_id, numerus positio, Decodere m) → tensor.Tensor ⇥ DecodeError {
    si token_id < 0 aut token_id ≥ m.vocabulum() {
        iace finge IdExtra { causa = "token id out of vocabulary range" }
    }
    si positio < 0 aut positio ≥ m.contextus() {
        iace finge PositioInvalida { causa = "position out of context" }
    }
    fixum lista<f32> row ← _immersio(m.mensa(), token_id, m.dimensio())
    fixum tensor.Tensor x ← _tense(row, [1, m.dimensio()])
    fixum tensor.Tensor h ← _bloccum(m, x, [positio])
    fixum tensor.Tensor logits ← _projicere(m, h)
    # The [1, V] projection flattens to the full-vocab logits [V].
    redde _tense(logits.datos, [m.vocabulum()])
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# praefundere — the multi-token (teacher-forced) path: prompt token ids →
# full-vocab logits [N, V] over the SAME forward functions as decode.
# The prompt length must not exceed the context limit (reject policy).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

functio praefundere(lista<numerus> tokens, Decodere m) → tensor.Tensor ⇥ DecodeError {
    si tokens.longitudo() ≡ 0 {
        iace finge ElementaMismatch { causa = "empty prompt" }
    }
    si tokens.longitudo() > m.contextus() {
        iace finge PositioInvalida { causa = "prompt exceeds the context limit" }
    }
    itera ex tokens fixum t {
        si t < 0 aut t ≥ m.vocabulum() {
            iace finge IdExtra { causa = "token id out of vocabulary range" }
        }
    }
    varia lista<f32> flat ← vacua
    itera ex tokens fixum t {
        fixum lista<f32> row ← _immersio(m.mensa(), t, m.dimensio())
        itera ex row fixum v {
            flat.appende(v)
        }
    }
    fixum tensor.Tensor x ← _tense(flat, [tokens.longitudo(), m.dimensio()])
    varia lista<numerus> positions ← vacua
    itera ab 0‥tokens.longitudo() fixum i {
        positions.appende(i)
    }
    fixum tensor.Tensor h ← _bloccum(m, x, positions)
    redde _projicere(m, h)
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sessio — the explicit session position state. Reset and the context
# limit are explicit public behaviors: progredere rejects at the limit,
# redintegra resets to position 0. No hidden position state.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
genus Sessio {
    numerus positio
    numerus contextus

    # The next decode position.
    functio positio() → numerus {
        redde ego.positio
    }

    # The session's context limit.
    functio contextus() → numerus {
        redde ego.contextus
    }
}

# A fresh session at position 0 with the declared context limit.
@ publica
functio sessio_fresh(numerus contextus) → Sessio ⇥ DecodeError {
    si contextus < 1 {
        iace finge DecodereInvalida { causa = "context length must be at least one" }
    }
    redde Sessio { positio = 0, contextus = contextus }
}

# Advance the session by one position — rejects when the next position
# would be at or beyond the context limit (the limit is reached).
functio progredere(Sessio s) → Sessio ⇥ DecodeError {
    si s.positio() + 1 ≥ s.contextus() {
        iace finge Terminus { causa = "context limit reached" }
    }
    redde Sessio { positio = s.positio() + 1, contextus = s.contextus() }
}

# Reset the session to position 0 (fresh state).
@ publica
functio redintegra(Sessio s) → Sessio {
    redde Sessio { positio = 0, contextus = s.contextus() }
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cancellation observation — the cooperative checkpoint (PML5-U5).
# Cancelatum is an explicit pure value the generation loop owns; the
# observation point (observa_cancellationem) is the cooperative check the
# loop calls at step boundaries. Cancellation is cooperative and fail
# closed: the flag is observed, never assumed, and a set flag rejects with
# a typed Cancelata — no silent mid-decode abort, no ignored cancellation.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ publica
genus Cancelatum {
    bivalens cancellata

    # The cancellation flag (true = cancellation requested).
    functio cancellata() → bivalens {
        redde ego.cancellata
    }
}

# A fresh (not cancelled) cancellation token.
@ publica
functio cancelatum_fresh() → Cancelatum {
    redde Cancelatum { cancellata = falsum }
}

# A cancellation-requested token.
functio cancelatum_cancellata() → Cancelatum {
    redde Cancelatum { cancellata = verum }
}

# The cooperative checkpoint: when the flag is set the step REJECTS with
# Cancelata (fail closed — no silent skip); otherwise the token passes
# through unchanged (the loop continues).
@ publica
functio observa_cancellationem(Cancelatum c) → Cancelatum ⇥ DecodeError {
    si c.cancellata() {
        iace finge Cancelata { causa = "cancellation requested" }
    }
    redde c
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# replica — the deterministic replay composition (PML5-U5). A bounded
# sampling loop: each logits row is drawn via sampling.sors with the
# running history and the explicit Semen state (which advances); the drawn
# token appends to the history and the outcome list. Pure — equal inputs
# (same logits stream, config, history, seed, cancellation flag) produce
# equal token sequences. Cancellation is observed at the entry and before
# every step (the cooperative checkpoint). The model decode (logits
# production) is NOT part of this composition — U6 wires decodere_datum
# in. Sampling errors map to SamplingDefecta (the causa text preserved).
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ privata
functio _mappa_sampling(sampling.SamplingError e) → DecodeError {
    redde finge SamplingDefecta { causa = sampling.causa(e) }
}

functio replica(lista<lista<f32>> logita, sampling.Configura c, lista<numerus> historia, train.Semen semen, Cancelatum cancelatum) → lista<numerus> ⇥ DecodeError {
    fixum Cancelatum _ ← observa_cancellationem(cancelatum)
    varia lista<numerus> result ← vacua
    varia lista<numerus> running ← vacua
    itera ex historia fixum t {
        running.appende(t)
    }
    varia train.Semen current ← semen
    itera ex logita fixum row {
        fixum Cancelatum _ ← observa_cancellationem(cancelatum)
        varia sampling.Sortitio outcome
        fac {
            outcome ← sampling.sors(row, c, running, current)
        }
        cape err {
            iace _mappa_sampling(err)
        }
        fixum numerus token ← outcome.token_id()
        result.appende(token)
        running.appende(token)
        current ← outcome.semen()
    }
    redde result
}
